APPCAST.XML MAINTENANCE GUIDE
==============================

This file provides update information to WinSparkle for auto-updates.
It should be hosted at a stable URL (e.g., https://iina.io/appcast.xml).

Field Descriptions:
-------------------

<title> - Version name shown to users
<sparkle:releaseNotesLink> - URL to release notes (GitHub release page recommended)
<pubDate> - Publication date in RFC 822 format
<enclosure url> - Direct download URL to the installer (.exe)
<sparkle:version> - Version number (must match CMakeLists.txt version)
<sparkle:shortVersionString> - User-visible version string
<length> - File size in bytes (get with: (Get-Item installer.exe).Length)
<type> - MIME type (always "application/octet-stream" for .exe)
<sparkle:os> - Target OS (always "windows-x64" for our builds)
<sparkle:minimumSystemVersion> - Minimum Windows version (10.0.0 = Windows 10)

How to Add a New Release:
--------------------------

1. Build and test the new version
2. Upload installer to GitHub Releases:
   - Tag: v0.2.0
   - File: IINA-Windows-0.2.0-Setup.exe

3. Get the file size:
   PowerShell: (Get-Item IINA-Windows-0.2.0-Setup.exe).Length
   Output: 52428800

4. Add new <item> block at the TOP of the channel (newest first)

5. Update fields:
   - <title>Version 0.2.0</title>
   - <sparkle:releaseNotesLink>https://github.com/iina/iina-windows/releases/tag/v0.2.0</sparkle:releaseNotesLink>
   - <pubDate>$(Get-Date -Format 'ddd, dd MMM yyyy HH:mm:ss +0000')</pubDate>
   - <enclosure url>https://github.com/iina/iina-windows/releases/download/v0.2.0/IINA-Windows-0.2.0-Setup.exe</enclosure>
   - sparkle:version="0.2.0"
   - sparkle:shortVersionString="0.2.0"
   - length="52428800"

6. Validate XML:
   - Check well-formedness: https://www.xmlvalidation.com/
   - Test in WinSparkle: Run app and check for updates

7. Deploy:
   - Upload appcast.xml to your web server
   - Ensure URL matches what's in autoupdate.cpp initialize() call
   - Verify HTTPS is used (required for security)

Important Notes:
----------------
- ALWAYS use HTTPS for security
- Keep items in reverse chronological order (newest first)
- File size MUST be accurate (WinSparkle verifies downloads)
- Version comparison is alphanumeric (0.2.0 > 0.1.0, but 0.10.0 > 0.2.0)
- Test updates on a clean VM before releasing

Automation with CI/CD:
----------------------
See .github/workflows/release.yml for automated appcast generation.
The workflow can auto-update this file when creating GitHub releases.

Security:
---------
- Sign installers with Authenticode for production releases
- Use HTTPS for appcast URL (prevents MITM attacks)
- Consider adding sparkle:dsaSignature for extra verification

Example CI/CD appcast generation:
```powershell
$version = "0.2.0"
$url = "https://github.com/iina/iina-windows/releases/download/v$version/IINA-Windows-$version-Setup.exe"
$length = (Get-Item "IINA-Windows-$version-Setup.exe").Length
$date = Get-Date -Format "ddd, dd MMM yyyy HH:mm:ss +0000"

# Insert into appcast.xml programmatically
```

